# Habit Tracker Development Guidelines

## TypeScript & Component Architecture

- **Always use TypeScript**: All files must have proper type definitions
- **Small, focused components**: Each component should have a single responsibility
- **Type safety**: Define interfaces for all props and data structures
- **No `any` types**: Use proper types or `unknown` with type guards

## Development Principles

- **Follow @anti-pitfall-guidelines**: Apply MVP-first, dependency-aware, iterative approach
- **Stay within MVP scope**: Refer to @.cursor/plans/habit-tracker-mvp.md for approved features
- **Avoid scope creep**: Features listed in "Out of Scope" section should not be implemented


## Component Guidelines

- Keep components under 150 lines when possible
- Extract reusable logic into utility functions
- Use React hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`, `useMemo`) appropriately
- Prefer composition over complex prop drilling
